@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+> **Update:** the byte-exact 76-byte placeholder technique described here was replaced by `pdf.BuildPDF`, which computes the xref offsets and `/Length` at build time. The old template declared `/Length 120` for a 151-byte stream (qpdf reported damage) and failed for BASE_URLs longer than 48 characters. Kept for historical interest.
+
 # 01 — Byte-Exact PDF Substitution
 
 ## The Problem: PDF Cross-Reference (xref) Offsets
diff -ruN '--exclude=node_modules' '--exclude=dist' '--exclude=.git' '--exclude=pnpm-lock.yaml' a/learn/03_mysql_wire_protocol_honeypot.md b/learn/03_mysql_wire_protocol_honeypot.md
--- a/learn/03_mysql_wire_protocol_honeypot.md	2026-10-14 02:25:23.000000000 +0000
+++ b/learn/03_mysql_wire_protocol_honeypot.md	2026-10-16 20:22:49.317014453 +0000
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+> **Update:** attribution is now by exact match of the full token ID encoded in the username (`svc_<24 hex>`). The previous truncated `canary_<12>` username never matched and connections fell back to an arbitrary recent MySQL token. Packets are capped at 64 KiB before allocation, connections are limited, and client attributes (`_client_name`, `_client_version`...) plus planted-password verification are recorded.
+
 # 03 — MySQL Wire Protocol Honeypot
 
 ## Why a Custom Protocol Implementation?
diff -ruN '--exclude=node_modules' '--exclude=dist' '--exclude=.git' '--exclude=pnpm-lock.yaml' a/learn/06_event_dedup_and_geo_enrichment.md b/learn/06_event_dedup_and_geo_enrichment.md
--- a/learn/06_event_dedup_and_geo_enrichment.md	2026-10-14 02:26:40.000000000 +0000
+++ b/learn/06_event_dedup_and_geo_enrichment.md	2026-10-16 20:22:49.317398462 +0000
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+> **Update:** de-duplication is atomic (`SET NX`) and keyed by token + IP + *class* (`hit` vs `fp`), so the browser-fingerprint alert is no longer suppressed by the initial hit. The window is fixed (5 min), not sliding. Pagination is `LIMIT/OFFSET`, not cursor-based.
+
 # 06 — Event Pipeline, GeoIP & Deduplication
 
 ## The Threat of Notification Storms
